  "raw_response": "Looking at the examples, I need to find the rule:\n\n1. The grid is divided into 3\u00d73 blocks separated by rows/columns of 5s.\n2. Exactly one block contains no 8s \u2014 this is the \"template\" block.\n3. Each value in the template block at position (r,c) determines what fills the entire block at meta-position (r,c) in the output.\n\n```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Extract 3x3 blocks (separated by 5s at row 3, col 3, etc.)\n    blocks = {}\n    block_positions = []\n    for br in range(3):\n        for bc in range(3):\n            r0 = br * 4\n            c0 = bc * 4\n            block = []\n            for r in range(3):\n                row = []\n                for c in range(3):\n                    row.append(grid[r0 + r][c0 + c])\n                block.append(row)\n            blocks[(br, bc)] = block\n            block_positions.append((br, bc))\n    \n    # Find the block that contains no 8\n    template = None\n    for pos in block_positions:\n        has_8 = any(blocks[pos][r][c] == 8 for r in range(3) for c in range(3))\n        if not has_8:\n            template = blocks[pos]\n            break\n    \n    # Build output: each meta-block (br, bc) is filled with template[br][bc]\n    result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    for br in range(3):\n        for bc in range(3):\n            val = template[br][bc]\n            r0 = br * 4\n            c0 = bc * 4\n            for r in range(3):\n                for c in range(3):\n                    result[r0 + r][c0 + c] = val\n    \n    # Keep separator rows/cols as 5\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 5:\n                result[r][c] = 5\n    \n    return result\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Extract 3x3 blocks (separated by 5s at row 3, col 3, etc.)\n    blocks = {}\n    block_positions = []\n    for br in range(3):\n        for bc in range(3):\n            r0 = br * 4\n            c0 = bc * 4\n            block = []\n            for r in range(3):\n                row = []\n                for c in range(3):\n                    row.append(grid[r0 + r][c0 + c])\n                block.append(row)\n            blocks[(br, bc)] = block\n            block_positions.append((br, bc))\n    \n    # Find the block that contains no 8\n    template = None\n    for pos in block_positions:\n        has_8 = any(blocks[pos][r][c] == 8 for r in range(3) for c in range(3))\n        if not has_8:\n            template = blocks[pos]\n            break\n    \n    # Build output: each meta-block (br, bc) is filled with template[br][bc]\n    result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    for br in range(3):\n        for bc in range(3):\n            val = template[br][bc]\n            r0 = br * 4\n            c0 = bc * 4\n            for r in range(3):\n                for c in range(3):\n                    result[r0 + r][c0 + c] = val\n    \n    # Keep separator rows/cols as 5\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 5:\n                result[r][c] = 5\n    \n    return result",
